// Same ally-targeting issue as cure_wounds (`SelfBuff` can't land on anyone
// but the caster -- see that file's header), but the sheet's second problem
// is range: it wants a ranged single-ally heal at 18m, not touch. Checked
// for a ranged-ally-target primitive: `ProjectileAttack.attack_effect`
// (common/src/comp/projectile.rs) is hardcoded to `GroupTarget::OutOfGroup`
// at construction time regardless of the `friendly_fire` flag (which only
// widens the plain `damage`/poise/knockback targeting, not the custom
// `attack_effect` a heal would need) -- no existing spell delivers a custom
// effect onto an ally at range. Ships touch-range instead, same
// `BasicMelee` + `InGroup` pattern as cure_wounds, a documented
// simplification rather than new engine work. The `Bonus` cast_time (quick
// heal) and a smaller heal than cure_wounds are kept as the mechanical
// differentiation between the two spells, matching their D&D relationship.
BasicMelee(
    energy_cost: 25.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.25,
    swing_duration: 0.1,
    hit_timing: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    melee_constructor: (
        kind: Stab(damage: 1, poise: 0, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
        range: 3.0,
        angle: 20.0,
        attack_effect: Some((
            Heal(26.0),
            AttackSource(Melee),
        )),
        attack_effect_target: Some(InGroup),
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Divine)),
)
